# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orbit — GST e-invoicing (IRP) credentials
#
# Copy the vars you need into your main .env to switch Orbit's invoice
# finalization from the deterministic SANDBOX/MOCK IRN to a LIVE IRN registered
# on the NIC Invoice Registration Portal (IRP) via your GSP.
#
# Behaviour:
#   • ALL five IRP_BASE_URL / IRP_CLIENT_ID / IRP_CLIENT_SECRET / IRP_USERNAME /
#     IRP_PASSWORD set  → live IRP call (falls back to mock on any error).
#   • Any of them missing → deterministic mock IRN (dev/demo safe).
#
# See lib/irp.ts (IRP_SETUP_DOC) for the full walkthrough.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of your GSP / IRP API.
#   NIC sandbox: https://einv-apisandbox.nic.in
#   or your GSP's sandbox / production host.
# IRP_BASE_URL=https://einv-apisandbox.nic.in

# GSP client credentials — sent as the "client_id" / "client_secret" headers.
# IRP_CLIENT_ID=your-gsp-client-id
# IRP_CLIENT_SECRET=your-gsp-client-secret

# IRP API user — "user_name" header; password is used to fetch the AuthToken.
# IRP_USERNAME=your-irp-api-username
# IRP_PASSWORD=your-irp-api-password

# (Optional) Pre-fetched AuthToken for quick sandbox testing. In production the
# adapter should fetch + cache this from the IRP /auth endpoint instead.
# IRP_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Where to get sandbox credentials ──
# 1. Register on the NIC e-invoice sandbox (https://einv-apisandbox.nic.in) with a
#    test GSTIN, OR
# 2. Onboard with a licensed GSP (ClearTax, Masters India, IRIS, Zoho, TaxPro,
#    Cygnet, …) — they issue client_id/client_secret + API user creds.
